<p>The goblet. Silver, ancient. The potion shifts between colours   silver, violet, near-black. But there's a difference I notice   a thread of deep amber winding through the iridescence, a colour that wasn't present in Ilara's earlier descriptions. The partial form. A different recipe. A different instruction set for the magic.</p>

<p>I drink. The taste is the same   iron, flowers, the unnamed thing that registers in the blood. But beneath it, something warmer. A bass note. A rumble. As if the potion carries two frequencies and my body is being asked to harmonise with both simultaneously.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">ILARA</span>"The Rite of Becoming begins. Partial Form. May the Mother accept this offering and return it transformed   and honour that which is preserved."</div>

<p>The chanting starts. The runes flare. The stars spin.</p>

